 "description": "Audit record of the SP1/RISC Zero ports (zkvm.rs) of the NPBench/Pythran entry functions in the zkVM performance set (eval-npbench, 2026-10-07; checklist and findings in eval-redo/fix/eval-npbench.md). An entry covers the zkvm.rs with that SHA-256; a changed file must be reviewed again. `excluded` names ports that must not be measured, with the reason.",
 "checklist": [
  "Q32 integer arithmetic (no f64/f32), with Zinnia's rounding (floor products, Euclidean division, contractions rescaled once)",
  "shapes from the fixture (the acceptance signature, cap 16), committed with the outputs and checked by the host",
  "the same function as kernel.py (body verbatim upstream), same evaluation order",
  "outputs public (committed), equal to NumPy position by position on inputs A and B within the case tolerance (native, SP1 and RISC Zero executors)",
  "inputs private; parameters the kernel never reads are not sent (as Zinnia drops them)",
  "no dead work, no skipped work, idiomatic Rust (direct indexing, loops, ndarray)",
  "preconditions asserted; NumPy errors panic"
 ],
